FIXED: Blackboxes now render in a fresh identifier scope per HDL module: local identifiers no longer accumulate `_N` suffixes across modules, making names generated by template functions (e.g. VIO/ILA probe names) predictable. See [#2722](https://github.com/clash-lang/clash-compiler/issues/2722).

CHANGED: All identifier creation functions in `Clash.Netlist.Id` now take a `Scope` (`Local` or `Global`) as their first argument, stating whether the name must remain unique for the entire design or only within the HDL module being rendered. Template functions should migrate `Id.make "x"` to `Id.make Local "x"`. The `IdentifierSetMonad` and `HasIdentifierSet` classes have been replaced by `IdentifierScopesMonad` and `HasIdentifierScopes`.
